Ladybird applies the frame’s no, noscroll, or off attribute value to
the child viewport. WebKit’s HTMLFrameElementBase::scrollingMode and
LocalFrame::updateScrollingMode carry that choice to its view. Blink
parses the owner’s attribute in HTMLFrameElementBase::ParseAttribute
and uses the mode in LayoutView::CalculateScrollbarModes. Gecko maps
the attribute in nsGenericHTMLFrameElement and applies the scrollbar
preference in ScrollContainerFrame::GetScrollStyles.

Chrome 158.0.8127.36, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 scrolled the
page for all three spellings, including mixed case. The child took the
wheel for yes, an unknown value, and an omitted attribute. Changing the
attribute changed which viewport took the next gesture.
